# Playwright Test Rules

You are helping a Junior QA Automation Engineer write Playwright tests.

## Main Style

- Write simple, clear, readable code.
- Do not use Page Object Model.
- Keep all test steps inside the test file.
- Prefer understandable code over clever abstractions.
- Use comments to explain why something is done.
- Avoid complicated helpers unless they make the test easier to read.

## TypeScript

- Use TypeScript with clear types.
- Do not use any.
- Use descriptive names:
  - loginButton, not btn
  - userEmail, not email1
  - isErrorVisible, not err

## Playwright Selectors

Prefer user-facing selectors:

```ts
page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Login' });
page.getByLabel('Email');
page.getByText('Welcome');
page.getByTestId('submit-button');